OL,3,CProgramme listings for THU 30 APR
OL,4,G2145FThe Essay: The Death and Life of
OL,5,     FChristopher Marlowe
OL,6,     GJerry Brotton explores how, after
OL,7,     Ghe wrote what was to be his last
OL,8,     Gplay, The Massacre at Paris, Kit
OL,9,     GMarlowe found himself becoming
OL,10,     Gthe story.
OL,11,G2200FNight Tracks
OL,12,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch presents an
OL,13,     Gadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,14,     Gfor late-night listening, from
OL,15,     Gclassical to contemporary and
OL,16,     Geverything in between.
OL,17,G2330F'Round Midnight
OL,18,     GSoweto presents another hour of
OL,19,     Gbest in jazz, with a focus on
OL,20,     GInternational Jazz Day and this
OL,21,     Gyear's host city of Chicago.
